# Factory-tree /etc/shadow, copied into the /etc subvol on first boot by
# tmpfiles C!; later passwd edits persist across image upgrades.
#
# NINE colon-separated fields. The third (lastchg) is deliberately EMPTY,
# which disables password aging — and keeps the build reproducible, since
# any real date would have to be recomputed per build. An 8-field line
# shifts min/max/warn left: lastchg=0 means "must change at next login",
# min=99999 then refuses that change, and login becomes impossible. That
# shipped for one release and only surfaced once /etc/shadow started
# coming live from the factory tree through the overlay.
#
# root ships the bootstrap password `changeme` — the only credential in the
# image, since no interactive user is provisioned. Console-only: sshd is
# publickey-only, and the documented flow ends in `passwd -l root`.
# See README "Post-installation". Override per fleet via mkosi.local.conf
# ExtraTrees=. Interactive users are owned by systemd-homed, not seeded here.
